What:           /sys/class/backlight/apple_studio_display*/physical_device
What:           /sys/bus/iio/devices/iio:device*/physical_device
Date:           November 2026
Contact:        https://github.com/eva-val/hid-apple-studio-display/issues
Description:
                Read-only symlink to the physical USB device belonging to an
                Apple Studio Display. The IIO link is provided on devices named
                apple_studio_display_orientation, owned by this driver.

                Backlight and orientation devices for the same physical display
                resolve this link to the same canonical sysfs directory. That
                directory supplies standard USB identity attributes (idVendor,
                idProduct and serial) and contains the display's HID interfaces.
                Ambient-light IIO devices supplied by hid-sensor-als are already
                descendants of this USB device; this driver does not take them
                over or change their ABI. Walk their device ancestry to associate
                them with the same physical display.

                The backlight's parent remains its DRM connector when matched,
                independently of this physical identity. A backlight registered
                without a DRM match still links to its physical USB device.
                No ordering of backlight or IIO device numbers is implied.

                The links exist for the registered class devices' lifetime and
                are removed on driver unbind or USB disconnect. Device numbers
                and paths can change after reconnecting; enumerate again and
                use the USB serial when a persistent user preference is needed.
                These links carry identity only, with no desktop policy or
                requirement to run any userspace service.
